notes: |
  Aggressive compaction on mobile (≤720px) to make the editor
  genuinely usable — follow-up to wavecode-toast-overhead-and-
  toolbar-toggle which left the editor at 14 visible lines
  (was 1-2 before any fix). User still complained it was
  squished.

  Fixes (5 layered):
  1. cm-content font 11px → 10px (--fs-2xs), line-height
     1.4 → 1.3. cm-host ~216px shows 25 lines (was 14).
  2. Sheet snap heights: peek 35→30vh, half 50→40vh,
     full 70→65vh. Default --sheet-h 50→40vh. Saves 90px
     (half) / 45px (full) on 900vh viewport.
  3. Mobile fixed rows more compact: preset-row 44→32px,
     controls-row 52→44px. .app-body padding-top 96→76px
     on mobile.
  4. .score-panel max-height formula updated to use new
     --sheet-h default (40vh instead of 50vh).
  5. **index.html critical-CSS sync** — found during
     browser verification. Inline `<style>` in index.html
     has un-layered `.app-preset-row { position: relative; ... }`
     which has higher CSS-Layers priority than the
     `@layer components` rule in bundled CSS. Without
     this sync, computed style showed `position: relative`
     despite components.css being correct. Updated inline
     rule to match new layered CSS.

